waydroid-host-stack: a GATT write longer than ATT_MTU - 3 goes out in parts.

The bridge wrote every guest value with bluer's write(), a write command
(type "command"), whatever the guest asked.  BlueZ refuses a command
longer than ATT_MTU - 3 (att.c encode_pdu), and turns a request of that
size into a prepared long write, which the Tesla VCSEC does not take.
Seen on the Pro1x with a Tesla's phone key, 2026-11-23: "gatt write
failed len=114 mtu=110", the add-key message of the pairing; the
51-byte writes before it went through.  Now the guest's write type is
passed on (request or command) and a value longer than ATT_MTU - 3 is
written in consecutive parts of that size, as a client that negotiated
this MTU writes it; the car reassembles by its own length prefix
(teslamotors/vehicle-command, ble.go Send).  Tests: cargo test
(discovery::gatt_write_chunks_fit_and_split); not yet at the car.  Ours
(fxtec-pro1x-guix, 2026-11-27), on d9a316e (MIT), after
waydroid-host-stack-shared-link-owners.patch.

